unicodeLinebreak is a port of the Rust crate unicode-linebreak
(https://github.com/axelf4/unicode-linebreak), version 0.1.5, by Axel
Forsman, to Meadow. Its tables and test cases are generated from that crate,
and the code that drives the tables is translated from the crate's source.

The crate is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and so is this
port: see LICENSE, or http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.

The data describes the Unicode Character Database, which is Copyright
Unicode, Inc. and distributed under the Unicode License
(https://www.unicode.org/license.txt).
